  "slug": "rv-parks-campgrounds",
  "name": "Morpho Lodging: RV Parks and Campgrounds",
  "description": "Independently owned RV parks, campgrounds and RV resorts in the US (not Maine) with roughly 40 to 150 sites, or a smaller park of 25+ sites that has added cabins, park models or glamping units. Often a family business, sometimes second or third generation, or an investor who bought for land value and cash flow; owner-operators frequently live on site. The owner or owner group makes the decisions and is reachable. Operating now, or opening within six months with funding. Does NOT qualify: franchised or flagged parks (KOA, Jellystone, Sun Outdoors, Thousand Trails, Encore), parks run by a third-party management company the owner cannot hire around, state, county, federal or municipal parks, mobile home or long-term-only communities, RV dealers, RV storage, RV rental platforms, booking platforms and directories, and concept-stage or unfunded developments. Site count must be verified from the website (a stated number, a site map, or a listing of sites and cabins).",
  "offer_context": "Morpho sells a fractional operations / COO retainer ($1,500+ a month): SOPs, reservation and site-assignment process, seasonal staffing and workamper onboarding, guest communication, reporting, and direct booking infrastructure, plus an AI visibility QuickScan. Buying signals: change of ownership, adding rental units or glamping, switching reservation systems, consolidator pressure, pre-season hiring, 'call to reserve' with no online booking, reviews about check-in confusion or unreturned calls.",
